Dear Ying,

Regarding moving the labels to the side, you can use the option "vertex.label.dist = 1" (try different numbers to see what looks best for you) within the plot_poppr_msn() function.

As for the legend, I am not sure of how to fix via the plot_poppr_msn() function, but you could try hiding the legend completely (by setting "pop.leg = FALSE") and adding a new legend using base graphics. I attach an example below.

library(poppr)
data(Pinf)

Pinf_dist <- diss.dist(Pinf)
pinf_filtered <- filter_stats(Pinf, distance = Pinf_dist, plot = FALSE)
mlg.filter(Pinf, distance = diss.dist, algorithm = "n") <- 6

Pinf_msn <- poppr.msn(Pinf, distmat = Pinf_dist, showplot = FALSE)

set.seed(1)
plot_poppr_msn(Pinf, Pinf_msn, mlg=TRUE,
               gadj = 0.7,
               nodescale = 25,
               cutoff = NULL,
               quantiles = FALSE,
               beforecut = TRUE,
               pop.leg = FALSE, # hide pop legend
               size.leg = FALSE,
               scale.leg = TRUE,
               vertex.label.dist = 1, # move labels to the side
               palette = cm.colors(n = 2)
)

legend("topleft",legend=c(levels(pop(Pinf))), fill=cm.colors(n=2))

Hope it helps.

